{"url": "https://webaim.org/articles/pour/robust", "silo": "webaim", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n\t\t<title>WebAIM: Constructing a POUR Website - Robust</title>\n\t<link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"/media/favicon.ico\">\n\t<link rel=\"home\" href=\"/\">\n\t<link rel=\"search\" href=\"/search/\">\n\t<link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://webaim.org/blog/feed\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"WebAIM Blog\">\n\n\t<script async=\"\" src=\"https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-Y41PF8WV9X\"></script>\n\t<script>\n  \twindow.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\n  \tfunction gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}\n  \tgtag('js', new Date());\n  \tgtag('config', 'G-Y41PF8WV9X');\n\t</script>\n\t\n\t<link href=\"/styles/main.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\">\n\t<link href=\"/styles/print.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"print\">\n\t<script src=\"/media/scripts/jquery.js\"></script>\n\t<script src=\"/media/scripts/main.js\"></script>\n\t<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Roboto:400\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\">\n\t<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Kameron:400,700\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\">\n\t<link href=\"/styles/documents.css?ver=2\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\t\t<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Open+Sans:400,400i,700\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n<!--[if lt IE 9]>\n\t<script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"http://html5shiv.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/html5.js\"></script>\n<![endif]-->\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async=\"\" src=\"https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net/pagead/viewthroughconversion/1069381703/?random=1774677467611&amp;cv=11&amp;fst=1774677467611&amp;bg=ffffff&amp;guid=ON&amp;async=1&amp;en=gtag.config&amp;gtm=45je63p1v899903185za200zd899903185xec&amp;gcd=13l3l3l3l1l1&amp;dma=0&amp;tag_exp=0~115616985~115938465~115938469~117484252&amp;u_w=1080&amp;u_h=600&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwebaim.org%2Farticles%2Fpour%2Frobust&amp;frm=0&amp;tiba=WebAIM%3A%20Constructing%20a%20POUR%20Website%20-%20Robust&amp;hn=www.googleadservices.com&amp;npa=0&amp;pscdl=noapi&amp;auid=1598495543.1774677300&amp;uaa=x86&amp;uab=64&amp;uafvl=Chromium%3B145.0.7632.6%7CNot%253AA-Brand%3B99.0.0.0&amp;uamb=0&amp;uam=&amp;uap=Linux&amp;uapv=&amp;uaw=0&amp;data=event%3Dgtag.config&amp;rfmt=3&amp;fmt=4\"></script></head>\n<body>\n\n\n<div id=\"headcontainer\" class=\"clearfix\" style=\"background-image: url(/media/banners/articles.jpg)\">\n<header>\n\t<div id=\"skiptocontent\"><a href=\"#maincontent\">skip to main content</a></div>\n\t\n\t<h2><a href=\"/\"><img src=\"/media/logo.png\" width=\"630\" height=\"167\" alt=\"WebAIM - Web Accessibility In Mind\"></a></h2>\n\n\t<nav>\n\t\t<h2 class=\"hidden\">Main Navigation</h2>\n\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/services/\">Services</a></li>\n\t\t\t<li class=\"current\"><a href=\"/articles/\">Articles</a></li>\n\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/resources/\">Resources</a></li>\n\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/projects/\">Projects</a></li>\n\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/community/\">Community</a></li>\n\t\t</ul>\n\t</nav>\n\t<div id=\"search\">\n\t\t<form method=\"get\" role=\"search\" action=\"/search/\" id=\"sitesearch\">\n\t\t\t<p class=\"search\"><span><label for=\"q\">Search:</label> <input type=\"text\" name=\"q\" id=\"q\"><input type=\"image\" src=\"/media/template/search.svg\" alt=\"Submit Search\"></span></p>\n\t\t</form>\n\t\t\n\t\t<p class=\"intro\"><a href=\"/intro\">Introduction to Web Accessibility</a></p>\n\t\t\n\t\t<p class=\"training\"><a href=\"/services/training\">WebAIM Training</a></p>\n\t</div>\n\n</header>\n</div>\n\n<main id=\"maincontainer\" class=\"clearfix\">\n\n<article id=\"maincontent\">\n\n<h1>Constructing a POUR Website<br><span class=\"subtitle\">Robust</span></h1>\n\n<p id=\"breadcrumbs\"><span class=\"hidden\">You are here: </span><a href=\"/\">Home</a> &gt; <a href=\"/articles/\">Articles</a> &gt; <a href=\"./\">Constructing a POUR Website</a> &gt; Page 5: Robust</p>\n\n<nav role=\"navigation\">\n\t<h2>Article Contents</h2>\n\t<ol>\n\t\t<li>Page 1: <a href=\"./\">Putting People at the Center of the Process</a></li>\n\t\t<li>Page 2: <a href=\"perceivable\">Perceivable</a></li>\n\t\t<li>Page 3: <a href=\"operable\">Operable</a></li>\n\t\t<li>Page 4: <a href=\"understandable\">Understandable</a></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"currentpage\"><span class=\"hidden\">Current page: </span>Page 5: Robust\n\t\t\t<ol>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"#future\">Functionality Across Current and Future Technologies</a></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"#spec\">Using Technologies According to Specification</a></li>\n\t\t\t</ol>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ol>\n</nav>\n<div class=\"section\" id=\"future\">\n\t<h2>Functionality Across Current and Future Technologies</h2>\n\t<p>People bring various devices, operating systems, browsers, plugins, screen readers, and assistive hardware to the web\u2014and a wide variety of versions of all of those as well. Some users enable advanced features. Others turn them off. Some are eager early adopters of every new technology, some cling to the familiar until it stops working for them, and most are somewhere in between.</p>\n\t<p>Despite the differences between users and the technologies they use, they all expect the web to work. When they go to a site that does not support their technologies, they get frustrated and may never return. When users can choose their own technologies, this empowers them to tailor their technologies to their needs, including accessibility needs. Generally, the more control the user has, the more likely the user will be able to access the content effectively.</p>\n\t<p>Of course, reasonable limits apply to this logic. Designers and developers should not feel forced to accommodate outdated browsers that are no longer supported by their own creators. They should feel free to take advantage of technological advances, including in areas related to accessibility. When considering implementation of innovative technologies and techniques, they must strike a balance between pushing innovation boundaries and considering the technologies their end users will be using, employing graceful degradation where appropriate.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"section\" id=\"spec\">\n\t<h2>Using Technologies According to Specification</h2>\n\t<p>Typically, browsers accommodate some sloppy coding\u2014a missing <code>&lt;/p&gt;</code> tag will not crash the page, for example\u2014but they cannot correct or compensate for all errors and inconsistencies that developers introduce in web content. The best way to ensure that content displays properly and accessibly across browsers, platforms, and assistive technologies is to write <a href=\"//validator.w3.org/\">valid HTML</a> and ARIA.</p>\n\t<p>Rather than focus on the limitations of old technologies, it is often helpful to focus on the possibilities offered by current and future technologies. WebAIM's <a href=\"/projects/\">Screen Reader User Surveys</a> indicate that most screen reader users tend to use up-to-date browsers and screen readers, though there will always be some who lag. To create content that is compatible with future technologies, it is necessary to use current technologies according to specification, so that future browsers and assistive technologies will be able to interpret the content and facilitate the desired user experience.</p>\n</div>\n</article>\n<!--\n\t-->\n<aside id=\"articlemeta\">\n\n\t<div id=\"updated\">Last updated: <time datetime=\"2021-10-04\">Oct 4, 2021</time></div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<div id=\"related\">\n\t\t\t<h2>Related Resources</h2>\n\t\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/intro/\">Introduction to Web Accessibility</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/standards/wcag/checklist\">WCAG 2.0 Checklist</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/articles/visual/\">Visual Disabilities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/articles/auditory/\">Auditory Disabilities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/articles/motor/\">Motor Disabilities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/articles/cognitive/\">Cognitive Disabilities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/articles/seizure/\">Seizure Disorders</a></li>\n\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n</aside>\n</main>\n\n<footer>\n\t<div id=\"footerresources\">\n\t\t<div class=\"footerblock\">\n\t\t\t<h2 id=\"copyright\">\u00a92026 WebAIM</h2>\n\t\t\t<p id=\"contact\">\t\t\tUtah State University<br>\n\t\t\t6807 Old Main Hill<br>\n\t\t\tLogan, UT 84322-6807<br>\n\t\t\t<a class=\"phone\" href=\"tel:4357977024\">435.797.7024</a></p>\n\t\t\n\t\t<div id=\"checkpage\">\n\t\t\t<h2>Check Your Accessibility</h2>\n\t\t\t<form action=\"https://wave.webaim.org/report\" novalidate=\"\">\n\t\t\t\t<label for=\"waveurl\">Web site address:</label>\n\t\t\t\t<input type=\"url\" id=\"waveurl\" name=\"url\" title=\"Web site address\">\n\t\t\t\t<input type=\"submit\" value=\"WAVE\">\n\t\t\t</form>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"footerblock\">\n\t\t\t<h2 id=\"blog\">From the Blog</h2>\n\t\t\t<ul><li><a href=\"/blog/a-new-path/\">A New Path for Digital Accessibility?</a></li><li><a href=\"/blog/2026-predictions/\">2026 Predictions: The Next Big Shifts in Web Accessibility</a></li><li><a href=\"/blog/word-and-powerpoint-alt-text-roundup/\">Word and PowerPoint Alt Text Roundup</a></li><li><a href=\"/blog/accessibility-by-design/\">Accessibility by Design: Preparing K\u201312 Schools for What\u2019s Next</a></li></ul>\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"footerblock\">\n\t\t\t<h2 id=\"popular\">Popular Resources</h2>\n\t\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/services/training/\">WebAIM Training</a></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/standards/wcag/checklist\">WCAG 2 Checklist</a></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/newsletter\">WebAIM Monthly Newsletter</a></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/resources/contrastchecker\">Color Contrast Checker</a></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"/resources/designers/\">Web Accessibility for Designers</a></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li><a href=\"http://wave.webaim.org/\">WAVE Web Accessibility E